    "id": "p22-q38-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "38",
    "prompt": "Show that $\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)+\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)$ is equal to $$(\\sin\\alpha+\\cos\\alpha)(\\sin\\beta+\\cos\\beta).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(\\sin\\alpha+\\cos\\alpha)(\\sin\\beta+\\cos\\beta)=\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)+\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)$.\n\nExpand the product and recognise the sine sum and cosine difference expansions.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sin\\alpha+\\cos\\alpha)(\\sin\\beta+\\cos\\beta)&=\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta+\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\beta+\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\beta+\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta\\\\(\\sin\\alpha+\\cos\\alpha)(\\sin\\beta+\\cos\\beta)&=(\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\beta+\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\beta)+(\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta+\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta)\\\\(\\sin\\alpha+\\cos\\alpha)(\\sin\\beta+\\cos\\beta)&=\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)+\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
